<Layout title="Legal Updates in Spain | Employment & Immigration | Barcelona" description="Selected Spanish legal updates affecting employment and immigration matters, with links to official sources. López Márquez Abogados is based in Barcelona.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Legal updates" title="Selected legal changes in Spain, with the official source beside them." description="The point of this section is practical: identify changes that may affect an employment or immigration matter and send you to the primary source." primaryLabel="Contact the firm" primaryHref="/en/contact" note="The official publication prevails over this summary." />
<section class="section section-paper"><div class="container cards">
<article class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Employment · 30 September 2026</span><h2>Temporary employment measures for certain aid beneficiaries</h2><p>Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 introduced, in Article 36, a temporary restriction affecting certain companies receiving direct aid. The measure operates until 31 December 2026 and its scope depends on the company, aid and reason for the employment decision.</p></div><a class="link-arrow" href="/en/legal-updates/employment-measures-aid-beneficiaries-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the official BOE text →</a></article>
<article class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Employment · 15 September 2026</span><h2>Information and transparency of employment conditions</h2><p>Royal Decree 723/2026 develops Spanish rules on the information workers must receive about essential employment conditions and certain aspects of how those conditions are implemented.</p></div><a class="link-arrow" href="/en/legal-updates/employment-conditions-transparency-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the official BOE text →</a></article>
<article class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Immigration · April 2026</span><h2>Amendments to the Spanish Immigration Regulation</h2><p>Royal Decree 316/2026 amended several immigration rules, including matters connected with regularisation and family members of Spanish citizens.</p></div><div class="legal-update-links"><a class="link-arrow" href="/en/legal-updates/immigration-regulation-amendments-2026">Read our practical analysis →</a><a class="link-arrow" href="https://www.boe.es/eli/es/rd/2026/04/14/316" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the official BOE text →</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Immigration · 2 September 2026</span><h2>Shortage Occupation Catalogue · Q3 2026</h2><p>The catalogue can affect certain employment-based immigration applications when the occupation and the other statutory requirements match.</p></div><div class="legal-update-links"><a class="link-arrow" href="/en/legal-updates/shortage-occupation-catalogue-q3-2026">Read our practical analysis →</a><a class="link-arrow" href="https://www.boe.es/diario_boe/txt.php?id=BOE-A-2026-18504" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the official resolution →</a></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">How to use legal updates</span><h2>A news item is not a conclusion about your case.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Start with the date and official source, then compare the rule with the documents and circumstances of the actual matter. A change can be relevant without changing the legal position of every person or company.</p><p><a href="/en/resources">See the English resource library →</a></p></div></div></section>
<CTA title="Has a recent legal change affected your situation?" text="Tell us what changed, the relevant date and the employment or immigration issue you are dealing with." label="Contact the firm" />
</Layout>
